<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ibc0540a36f7cced00c6c3069a5ad57f006db8eb7" commit="e615d13074026bffa6d819daa2937b825978533f" commit_message="brillo_test_launcher: Check moblab version &amp; enable quickmerge by default  brillo_test_launcher will verify that the target MobLab is compatible with Brillo testing and if not will alert the user.  Also most test users want to use the latest code in their checkout, therefore swap the --quickmerge arg with --no_quickmerge.  BUG=b:26296251 TEST=local MobLab setup.  Change-Id: Ibc0540a36f7cced00c6c3069a5ad57f006db8eb7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319580 Commit-Ready: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gilad Arnold &lt;garnold@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319580" owner_email="sbasi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/80/319580/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0bbce8519c604212c178cdcf0c13334edf773db6" commit="27ce5739089cb3289d4454b8849c89f113584c79" commit_message="dut: Prevent unexpected stderr messages in ADB stdout.  The ADB protocol seem to have mixed stderr and stdout in same output channel so we can't simply grab stderr or ADB command (which will only get trace logs, if requested).  Currently there is no good solution yet so a quick solution is to always redirect stderr to /dev/null if that is not needed. In future we may improve that by utilizing temporary files.  BUG=chromium:557573 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I0bbce8519c604212c178cdcf0c13334edf773db6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320452 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320452" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/52/320452/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8b1471053484112bad8d872f707e01ac08fa2008" commit="23fd58662d36cec7a1d2a87e1e66f352b7ff7a19" commit_message="dut: improve the speed of AndroidPath.realpath  Since each &quot;adb shell&quot; command takes a long time, we are trying to reduce the overall &quot;adb shell&quot; command to make test cases faster.  1. Try 'realpath /entire/path' first, if succeeded, we are done. 2. Append each path component, one by one. If the component is '' (empty    string), '.' or '..' then we can solve it directly without calling    realpath.  BUG=None TEST=make test, also tested with an Android device  Change-Id: I8b1471053484112bad8d872f707e01ac08fa2008 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320588 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320588" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/88/320588/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I63bc70205627474590e38ffd282faedaea3bcc66" commit="9dba5d5e76e9f919b7196302612dedc6ce451b12" commit_message="pd: Add common EC_HOST_EVENT_PD_MCU implementation  For TCPMs with an off chip TCPC, PD MCU host event status can be handled in a common way. When a status flag is updated (ex. from charge_manager), notify the AP thr